---
import { TextSection } from '@components/odyssey-theme';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/sections/heros/HeroSection.astro';

const seo = {
	title: 'About | [summer larp]',
	description: 'Learn about [summer larp], the Bay Area music collective running a summer gigging circuit to raise funds for high-impact charitable causes.',
};
---

<Layout {seo}>
	<HeroSection>
		<div slot="text-container">
			<h1>About [summer larp]</h1>
			<p>
				A Bay Area music collective on a mission — playing shows, building community, and raising funds for causes that matter, one gig at a time.
			</p>
		</div>
    <picture slot="image-container">
      <img
        src="/assets/images/home/classic-hero.jpg"
        alt="[summer larp] collective performing"
        id="home-hero-image"
      />
    </picture>
	</HeroSection>

  <TextSection narrow>
    <h2>Our Story</h2>
    <p>
      [summer larp] started as a conversation between four friends — Vivan, Abhee, Ayaan, and Shashank — who wanted to make the most of a summer and use music as a vehicle for something bigger than a weekend jam session. The name is a nod to the spirit of it: a creative performance with purpose, not unlike live action role play, except the stakes are real and the music is louder.
    </p>
    <p>
      Based in the Tri-Valley (Pleasanton, Dublin, and Livermore), the collective draws from a rotating roster of over 20 musicians spanning bass, guitar, drums, vocals, keys, and a full horn section. Any given show might look slightly different depending on who's available and what the venue calls for — that flexibility is part of what makes [summer larp] work.
    </p>

    <h2>The Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Every show we play raises money for a charitable cause. But we're deliberate about which ones. Rather than defaulting to well-known brands, we seek out niche, high-impact initiatives that don't get the spotlight they deserve — local programs, under-resourced organizations, and causes that a live music audience might not have encountered before.
    </p>
    <p>
      We believe the collective can do more than entertain. Music is a natural meeting place. When you combine a great show with a meaningful cause, you get something that people remember and want to come back to. That's the idea behind [summer larp]: keep it fun, keep it real, and make it count.
    </p>

    <h2>The Circuit</h2>
    <p>
      The summer circuit runs 2–4 shows per week across the Bay Area, with a radius covering San Francisco, Oakland, Berkeley, San Jose, Marin, and Half Moon Bay. We prioritize venues with existing foot traffic — restaurants, downtown plazas, community festivals — places where music can reach people who weren't necessarily looking for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Want to have us play at your venue or event? Head to our <a href="/company/contact">Inquiry page</a> or find us on Instagram to start the conversation.
    </p>
  </TextSection>
</Layout>
